  "reasoning": "This commit (\"Fix race condition on TS3Query#io\") added `synchronized` to `connect()`, `exit()`, and `doCommandAsync()`, all locking on the same TS3Query instance monitor. This created a new deadlock/race hazard: `exit()` could be invoked concurrently from multiple threads (e.g., directly and via `fireDisconnect()`'s async task calling `exit()` again), with one thread blocked inside `exit()` waiting for `api.quit()` to complete (which itself requires `doCommandAsync` to acquire the same lock from the I/O thread). The fix commit directly overhauls this exact synchronization design—replacing the plain `synchronized` guard on `exit()` with atomic flags and proper wait/notify signaling—confirming that the locking scheme from c8156def8cdc was the root cause of the synchronization bug being fixed.",
